
Description:

MDN/parse (RFC 9007) is implemented; it was a stub that reported every
blob as notParsable.  MDN/send follows RFC 9007, Section 2.1: it takes
identityId and onSuccessUpdateEmail, accepts a client-set finalRecipient
and extensionFields, reports a missing message as notFound, and sends a
well-formed null envelope sender.  The MDN that the Sieve "reject" action
sends no longer doubles the address-type in Original-Recipient.


Documentation:

docsrc/rfc-support.rst lists RFC 9007.


Config changes:

None.


Upgrade instructions:

Clients of the earlier MDN/send must now pass identityId (the value
Identity/get reports) and an onSuccessUpdateEmail argument that sets the
$mdnsent keyword, as RFC 9007 requires.


GitHub issue:

None.
